---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DIG, SUPPORT, SERVICE } from "../config/brand";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — WOIII.me"
  description="Terms for using WOIII.me, an independent read-only pressing guide for Discogs, and the earlier DIG for Discogs service."
  bodyClass="privacy-page"
  headerVariant="overlay"
>
  <section class="section privacy-section" data-header-tone="dark">
    <div class="wrap policy">
      <h1>Terms of <span class="accent">Service</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These terms govern your use of {SERVICE.name}: its Chrome side panel
        extension, its plugin and connector for ChatGPT and Claude, and the
        server and API behind them. They also cover {SERVICE.formerName}, the
        earlier version.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Effective and last updated: 21 October 2026</p>

      <h2>Accepting these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By installing, connecting to or using {SERVICE.name}, you agree to these
        terms and the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not
        agree, do not use it, and revoke or remove any existing connection. You
        must be legally able to accept these terms and meet the age
        requirements of Discogs, your AI provider and the other services you
        use with {SERVICE.name}.
      </p>

      <h2>What {SERVICE.name} provides</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} is a free, read-only guide to vinyl pressings on Discogs.
        It scores and compares an album's pressings for sound or for
        collectors, explains the evidence behind each score, and can summarise
        your own collection and rank your wantlist. It never changes anything on
        your Discogs account, and it shows no marketplace prices, listings or
        cover images. Features may change, be limited or become unavailable.
      </p>

      <h2>Beta service</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} is in beta. Its server address may change, the service
        may be slow or unavailable at busy times (all users share one Discogs
        rate limit), and features may be added, changed or removed without
        notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Your accounts and authorisation</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the accounts and clients you connect, for
        keeping your credentials secure, and for activity authorised through
        your connection. Do not share tokens or connect an account you do not
        control. You can revoke {SERVICE.name} on Discogs and remove it from
        your browser or AI client at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not use {SERVICE.name} to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access private or restricted data without authorisation;</li>
        <li>bypass rate limits, access controls or technical safeguards, including by automating requests;</li>
        <li>scrape, bulk-export, resell or build a database from returned data;</li>
        <li>send malware, probe other users, interfere with the service or expose credentials;</li>
        <li>break applicable law or the terms and policies of Discogs, Google, OpenAI, Anthropic or another connected service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Discogs data</h2>
      <p>
        Data shown by {SERVICE.name} is provided by Discogs and is attributed
        with a "Data provided by Discogs" link to its source page. It is never
        more than six hours old when shown. Discogs data can be incomplete,
        user-contributed, delayed or wrong, and Discogs' own terms apply to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Scores are estimates, not advice</h2>
      <p>
        Scores, verdicts and rankings are estimates built from Discogs data and
        published pressing knowledge. They do not measure sound, condition,
        authenticity or value. {SERVICE.name} does not buy or sell records,
        contact sellers or handle payments. Nothing it shows is financial,
        appraisal, legal or other professional advice. Check important
        information before you act on it.
      </p>

      <h2>AI assistants</h2>
      <p>
        In ChatGPT or Claude, your AI provider writes the replies you see and
        decides when to call {SERVICE.name}. We are responsible for the data our
        tools return, not for the text your assistant writes around it. Your
        provider's terms apply to your use of its assistant.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} depends on Discogs, Cloudflare, Fly.io, Google, your AI
        provider and other software and network services. Their terms and
        privacy practices apply separately. Links and references do not imply
        endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>Open-source software</h2>
      <p>
        Source code we publish in <a href={DIG.repoUrl}>the public repository</a>{" "}
        is licensed under the licence stated there. That licence does not
        replace these terms for the hosted service or grant rights in
        third-party data, names or trademarks.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} is provided free of charge on an "as available" basis.
        We may update, suspend, restrict or discontinue features to protect
        users, comply with third-party requirements, maintain security or run
        the service. We may update these terms by publishing a revised version
        with a new date; continuing to use {SERVICE.name} after that means you
        accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, {SERVICE.name} is provided without
        warranties of availability, accuracy, fitness for a particular purpose
        or non-infringement, and {SERVICE.name} is not responsible for
        decisions, purchases, losses or third-party actions based on its
        output. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot
        legally be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may restrict or end access when reasonably necessary for security,
        abuse prevention, legal compliance, third-party requirements or a
        material breach of these terms. You may stop at any time by revoking
        {SERVICE.name} on Discogs, uninstalling the extension and removing the
        plugin or connector.
      </p>

      <h2>Discogs relationship</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} (formerly {SERVICE.formerName}) is an independent
        project. This application uses Discogs' API but is not affiliated with,
        sponsored or endorsed by Discogs. "Discogs" is a trademark of Zink
        Media, LLC.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a>.{" "}
        For product help, see <a href="/support">Support</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    --accent-hue: #c8ff9f;
    background: #000;
    padding-block: 170px 104px;
  }
  .privacy-section > .policy {
    --text-width: 62rem;
    width: min(100%, 1440px);
    max-width: 1440px;
    padding-inline: clamp(24px, 3.35vw, 48px);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 7);
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2.5);
    padding-top: calc(var(--space) * 4);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: calc(var(--space) * 1.5);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy li::marker {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .policy p {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2);
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-tertiary);
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .privacy-section {
      padding-block: 125px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
